[ti:(untitled)]
[ar:VESAHE · hkfaduio]
[al:Sanatan & Devotional]
[by:Radio Vaigyaaniq — draft timing, unverified]
[00:08.00]भाग ३: मच्छरी का उत्तर Bhāg 3: Machcharī kā Uttar (The Mosquito's Reply)
[00:10.67]तू अपने बलकान खातिर
[00:13.34]जो एक बूँद चूस आवे से..
[00:16.01]Tū apne balkān khātir
[00:18.67]jo ek bū̃d cūs āve se..
[00:21.34]For the sake of your children
[00:24.01]that one drop I come to sip..
[00:26.68]I do not come to disturb your meditation.
[00:29.35]I do not come to test your advaita.
[00:32.02]I come because my young are hungry.
[00:34.68]I come because a river of blood
[00:37.35]is to me what the Ganga is to you—
[00:40.02]sacred, sustaining, simple.
[00:42.69]You see a mosquito.
[00:45.36]I see motherhood.
[00:48.03]You see an itch.
[00:50.69]I see survival.
[00:53.36]इसके के आग लगे से
[00:56.03]जो तन्हें दूर भगावे से..
[00:58.70]Iske ke āg lage se
[01:01.37]jo tanheṅ dūr bhagāve se..
[01:04.04]May fire consume the one
[01:06.70]who drives me away..
[01:09.37]Not a curse—
[01:12.04]a cry.
[01:14.71]When you wave your hand,
[01:17.38]you are not protecting your jñāna.
[01:20.05]You are telling a mother:
[01:22.71]Your hunger does not belong here.
[01:25.38]Your body does not belong here.
[01:28.05]Your life is a disturbance to my peace.
[01:30.72]What kind of peace
[01:33.39]is built on pushing away
[01:36.06]the small, the hungry, the other?
[01:38.72]You chant vayam sādhanā asti—
[01:41.39]We are the practice.
[01:44.06]But your we did not include me.
[01:46.73]Your sādhanā did not include
[01:49.40]the weight of my belly,
[01:52.07]the urgency of my young,
[01:54.73]the ancient rhythm of this proboscis
[01:57.40]seeking what it needs to create life.
[02:00.07]You wanted advaita—
[02:02.74]the unbroken, the still, the grand.
[02:05.41]But advaita without karuṇā (compassion)
[02:08.08]is just another name for numbness.
[02:10.74]Let me teach you now,
[02:13.41]as I taught you then:
[02:16.08]Your blood is not yours alone.
[02:18.75]It belongs to the soil, the rain, the mango tree,
[02:21.42]and to me—
[02:24.09]to my children yet to be born.
[02:26.75]When I land on your arm,
[02:29.42]I am not breaking your meditation.
[02:32.09]I am completing it.
[02:34.76]Because meditation that excludes life
[02:37.43]is not meditation.
[02:40.10]It is escape.
[02:42.76]You asked for a mantra.
[02:45.43]I give it now:
[02:48.10]Let the one who is hungry
[02:50.77]be fed by you.
[02:53.44]Let the one who is small
[02:56.11]be seen by you.
[02:58.77]Let the one who annoys you
[03:01.44]be your guru.
[03:04.11]This is vayam.
[03:06.78]This is sādhanā.
[03:09.45]This is the only anthem.
[03:12.12]I do not need your praise.
[03:14.78]I do not need your gratitude.
[03:17.45]I only need your stillness
[03:20.12]when I come.
[03:22.79]If you can give that—
[03:25.46]if you can sit with open arm
[03:28.13]and let me take what I need—
[03:30.79]then you will know:
[03:33.46]तू ही मच्छरी है
[03:36.13]तू ही पंडित है
[03:38.80]तू ही बूँद है
[03:41.47]तू ही ब्रह्म है
[03:44.14]Tū hī machcharī hai
[03:46.80]tū hī paṇḍit hai
[03:49.47]tū hī bū̃d hai
[03:52.14]tū hī brahma hai
[03:54.81]You are the mosquito
[03:57.48]You are the scholar
[04:00.15]You are the drop
[04:02.81]You are Brahman
[04:05.48]दीमी दीमी हम्मmmmmm
[04:08.15]Dhīmī dhīmī hmmmmm
[04:10.82]Softly, softly… hmmmmm
[04:13.49]Not a threat.
[04:16.16]Not a curse.
[04:18.82]Just the sound of life
[04:21.49]continuing.
[04:24.16]If you hear it as mantra,
[04:26.83]you are free.
[04:29.50]If you hear it as disturbance,
[04:32.17]you are still a pandit
[04:34.83]who has not yet understood.
[04:37.50]भाग ४: आगे बढ़ायें Bhāg 4: Aage Badhāyen (Moving Forward)
[04:40.17]The Stillness
[04:42.84]अब न हाथ हिलावे
[04:45.51]अब न मन चिढ़ावे
[04:48.18]जो आए सो आए
[04:50.84]जो जाए सो जाए
[04:53.51]Ab na hāth hilāve
[04:56.18]ab na man chiṛhāve
[04:58.85]jo āe so āe
[05:01.52]jo jāe so jāe
[05:04.19]Now no hand waves away
[05:06.85]Now no mind is vexed
[05:09.52]What comes, let it come
[05:12.19]What goes, let it go
[05:14.86]The mosquito drinks. A single drop. Then another. The pandit feels the faint sting, the small weight, the brief intimacy of another life touching his own.
[05:17.53]He whispers:
[05:20.20]तेरा रक्त मेरा रक्त
[05:22.86]तेरा बच्चा मेरा बच्चा
[05:25.53]तेरी भूख मेरी भूख
[05:28.20]तेरा जीवन मेरा जीवन
[05:30.87]Terā rakta merā rakta
[05:33.54]terā baccā merā baccā
[05:36.21]terī bhūkh merī bhūkh
[05:38.87]terā jīvan merā jīvan
[05:41.54]Your blood is my blood
[05:44.21]Your child is my child
[05:46.88]Your hunger is my hunger
[05:49.55]Your life is my life
[05:52.22]The Buzzing Returns
[05:54.88]The mosquito, finished, rests on his hand. She does not buzz in question. She buzzes in affirmation—a low, steady hum, like a tanpura.
[05:57.55]दीमी दीमी हम्मmmmmm
[06:00.22]अब समझ गया रे पंडित
[06:02.89]अब समझ गया
[06:05.56]Dhīmī dhīmī hmmmmm
[06:08.23]ab samajh gayā re paṇḍit
[06:10.89]ab samajh gayā
[06:13.56]Softly, softly, hmmmmm
[06:16.23]Now you understand, O pandit
[06:18.90]Now you understand
[06:21.57]The pandit opens his eyes. He looks at the mosquito on his hand. He does not see a pest. He does not see a teacher. He sees simply: life touching life.
[06:24.24]He says:
[06:26.90]तू न आई थी मुझे सिखाने
[06:29.57]मैं न बैठा था तुझे जानने
[06:32.24]फिर भी कुछ हुआ
[06:34.91]वही सत्य है
[06:37.58]Tū na āī thī mujhe sikhāne
[06:40.25]maiṅ na baiṭhā thā tujhe jānne
[06:42.91]phir bhī kuch huā
[06:45.58]vahī satya hai
[06:48.25]You did not come to teach me
[06:50.92]I did not sit to know you
[06:53.59]Yet something happened
[06:56.26]That is the truth
[06:58.92]The Anthem Merges
[07:01.59]He remembers his Quantum Anthem—the fragments, the Sanskrit, the grand declarations. Now it sounds different.
[07:04.26]He hums, softly:
[07:06.93]Q U ANT U MAN THEM
[07:09.60]q u an TUM ANT HEM
[07:12.27]He smiles.
[07:14.93]यही अंत है
[07:17.60]यही हेम है
[07:20.27]यही संगम है
[07:22.94]यही ब्रह्म है
[07:25.61]Yahī ant hai
[07:28.28]yahī hem hai
[07:30.94]yahī saṅgam hai
[07:33.61]yahī brahma hai
[07:36.28]This is the edge
[07:38.95]This is the boundary
[07:41.62]This is the confluence
[07:44.29]This is Brahman
[07:46.95]The mosquito lifts. She hovers before his face for a moment—close enough that he feels the breeze of her wings.
[07:49.62]She says—or perhaps the wind says, or perhaps his own heart says:
[07:52.29]The Final Teaching
